  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/src/stock_sim_breaks.rs`: new `breaks_stock_edge(world, op)`. It is true for a 2D Chamfer whose source names the setup's stock (the stock, or picks off the stock).\n- `crates/app/src/stock_sim.rs` (`plan_program`): the program sim credits no edge-break record of such an op. A part under the stock's edge is judged sharp.\n- `crates/app/src/posting_sim.rs` (`judge_clause`):\n  - Gouge arm: the refusal also gets the `kept_moved` line (#1628), so it names the op and the part.\n  - Clean arm (review finding 1): when every op is covered, the gate runs `kept_moved` too. A cut too shallow for the sim's lattice is thus refused by name.\n- `docs/decisions/2308-stock-chamfer-no-credit.md`: the decision, the dropped options and the cost. It names #2313 for the stock-source Deburr gouge, which this PR does not fix.\n- The branch has `origin/main` at `3f41b8da6` (#2309) merged, with no conflicts.\n\n## Cause\n\n1. The #303 credit took the declared bevel of the stock's edge as part of the finished part, over all columns under that edge.\n2. A part added after generation under that edge was thus judged as bevelled. The sim found zero gouge cells.\n3. With a clean sim verdict, the live re-judge (`kept_moved`) did not run, and `G01 X35. Y-35. Z19.` posted along the edge of the added part.\n\nThe #1631 solid law forbids a stock-source chamfer to enter any part. No refusal, gouge check or collision check is removed or made weaker. The sim verdict stays a judge. The live re-judge is an added judge in the clean arm.\n\n## Readings\n\n- On `main`, the aligned 1 mm case posts with `G01 X35. Y-35. Z19.`. With the fix, aligned and quarter-turned stock are refused by the sim gouge plus `S1 now cuts part 'other' (... stock-source chamfer breaks into a part ...)`. The hair-turned stock (not judged by the sim) is refused by `kept_moved`.\n- A part added 0.05 mm into the chamfer's cut (x 30..34.05): with only the no-credit change it POSTED (mutation check on this head). With the clean-arm re-judge, it is refused by name on aligned and quarter-turned stock.\n- A part added clear of the cut (x 18..24) posts on all three turns.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `stock_chamfer_added_part::a_part_added_under_a_judged_stock_source_chamfer_is_refused_by_name` (aligned, quarter, hair; 1 mm cut)\n- `stock_chamfer_added_part::a_part_added_a_hair_under_a_judged_stock_source_chamfer_is_refused_by_name` (aligned, quarter; 0.05 mm cut)\n- `stock_chamfer_added_part::a_part_added_clear_of_a_stock_source_chamfer_still_posts` (aligned, quarter, hair)\n\n## Suites on head `498ba08b5` (debug, `-j 6 --test-threads=6`)\n\nAll green:\n\n| Suite | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `stock_chamfer_added_part` | 3 passed |\n| `stock_source_holes` | 9 passed |\n| `keep_law` | 31 passed |\n| `kept_parts_live` | 4 passed |\n| `edge_break_gate` | 5 passed |\n| `edge_break_bound` | 5 passed |\n| `circular_pick_law` | 5 passed |\n| `trochoid_law` | 7 passed |\n| `pocket3d_open_side` | 7 passed |\n| `post_not_judged` | 4 passed |\n| `setup_carry_credits` | 7 passed |\n| `setup_align_2d_kinds` | 8 passed |\n| `mill2d_b` | 9 passed |\n| `stock_source_cross_drill` | 6 passed |\n| `golden_cl` | 33 passed |\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean. `cargo fmt -p camcraft-app -- --check`: clean.\n\nNo legal program becomes refused: each \"posts\" case in the suites above still posts, the part-source chamfer and deburr of `edge_break_gate` included.\n\n## Order of refusal lines\n\nOn sim-judged stock, a stock-source chamfer that cuts a part deep enough for the lattice is refused by the sim gouge first, then the op line. After #2309, the `stock_source_holes` chamfer cases turn the stock 1e-6 rad, where the sim does not judge. No assert in this PR was changed for the order.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No run on a real control.\n- No GUI run, no full workspace build, no release lanes, no heavy lanes.\n- A stock-source Deburr that cuts a part still posts. That is #2313, also on `main`, and not in this PR.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Chamfer off the stock no longer posts when a part added after generation stands under the stock's edge, also for a cut of a few hundredths of a millimetre; the post refuses and names the operation and the part.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2308\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
